<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-what-to-serve-with-stuffed-onions">What to Serve With Stuffed Onions</h2>



<p>So you&rsquo;ve made your beautiful stuffed baked onions. They&rsquo;re tender, aromatic, and perfectly seasoned. But what should you serve alongside them to turn this into a complete meal?</p>



<p>Below are a few traditional and Mediterranean-inspired pairings to help you serve them the way they&rsquo;re enjoyed across T&uuml;rkiye:</p>



<p><strong>Pair them with a cool yogurt sauce:</strong> A creamy yogurt sauce is one of the most classic pairings to dolma-style dishes. My <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/yogurt-dill-sauce/">Yogurt Dill Sauce</a> adds a bright, herby note with lemon and fresh dill, while my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/easy-to-make-tzatziki-sauce-recipe/">Tzatziki Sauce Recipe</a> is a classic pairing with thick Greek yogurt, cucumber, and garlic.&nbsp;</p>



<p><strong>Add a refreshing salad:</strong> A crisp salad never disappoints. <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/turkish-shepherd-salad/">Turkish Shepherd Salad</a> is a traditional go-to with juicy tomatoes, cucumbers, and herbs, especially in the summer months. If you want something a bit more herby, <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/easy-tabbouleh-recipe/">Tabbouleh</a> is another option with lots of fresh herbs.</p>



<p><strong>Serve with rice or pilaf:</strong> To make this a little more filling, pair your stuffed onions with a starchy side dish. If you want a Turkish side, my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/moms-bulgur-pilaf/">Bulgur Pilaf</a> is a classic, or try my Vermicelli Rice, another staple you&rsquo;ll often see served alongside dishes like this in many Mediterranean restaurants. And if you want a gluten-free option, <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/lemon-quinoa/">Lemon Quinoa</a> brings a fresh, zesty note without overpowering the main dish.</p>
</div>



